"epic aside" is a notebook page
	<header level="1">
		&lt;epic-aside&gt;
		<header>The &lt;epic-aside&gt; element: a folded aside, a digression the main text can skip.</>
	</>

	<text class="lede" paragraph>A folded aside in prose: a digression the main text can skip. It draws an ivory panel headed "Aside: &lt;title&gt;"; the aside is its children.</>

	<!--
		no <ui-list class="spell-meta">:  its <ui-item>s take Spell UI's "item" style sheet name before the
		              epics pack's elements can, and live examples may draw unstyled (issue I9 of epic-components)
	-->
	<text class="meta" paragraph>For anyone reading or writing an epic page's markup, or changing this element.</>
	<text class="meta" paragraph>Its vocabulary (every name it uses): <link target="src-spell-epic-src-components-epic-aside-epicaside-en-ts" link="/epic/src/components/epic-aside/EpicAside.en.ts"><text title="epic/src/components/epic-aside/EpicAside.en.ts" code>EpicAside.en.ts</></>.</>
	<text class="meta" paragraph>Its component: <link target="src-spell-epic-src-components-epic-aside-epicaside-tsx" link="/epic/src/components/epic-aside/EpicAside.tsx"><text title="epic/src/components/epic-aside/EpicAside.tsx" code>EpicAside.tsx</></>, with its style sheet (<text code>.css</>) and tests beside it.</>

	<section label="1. Example">
		<icon slot="icon" name="eye"/>
		<text paragraph>A real one, from epic <text code>docs-workspace</> (O3). Click its heading to unfold it.</>
		<html>
			<epic-aside title="why a script, not hand edits?">
				<p>Ids, icons, UPDATE markers and the "updated" stamp must agree across the phase list, the phase sections and the items. Agents editing by hand drift; the script also locks the file so parallel agents take turns.</>
			</>
		</>
		<text class="meta" paragraph>Live: the real element, drawn by the epics pack this page loads.</>

		<section label="With buttons in its title row" sticky collapsible dividing open="false">
			<text paragraph>A page's own buttons go in its title row: <text code>&lt;ui-button slot="actions"&gt;</> children (epic <text code>epic-workflow</> P25).</>
			<list bulleted>
				<item>They sit at the right of the title row, after the heading. The heading is its fold button, and it ends where they start.</>
				<item>A click on one never folds or unfolds it.</>
				<item>The docs runtime puts the block's bullhorn there too, so it never sits over a button.</>
			</>
			<example "With buttons in its title row">
				<html>
					<epic-aside title="why a slot, not a float">
						<p>A button floated over the heading's corner sat on the fold button; in the row, each has its own room.</p>
						<ui-button slot="actions" appearance="circular basic" size="mini" icon="copy" title="Copy a link to it" aria-label="Copy a link to it"></ui-button>
					</epic-aside>
				</html>
			</example>
		</>
	</>

	<section label="2. Markup">
		<icon slot="icon" name="code"/>
		<text paragraph>From <link title="epics/docs-workspace/parts/o3.html" target="src-epics-docs-workspace-parts-o3-html" link="/epics/docs-workspace/parts/o3.html"><text code>o3.html</></>:</>
		<text paragraph>o3.html · its aside:</>
		<markdown>
			```html
			<epic-aside title="why a script, not hand edits?"
			  ><p>
			    Ids, icons, UPDATE markers and the "updated" stamp must agree across the phase list, the phase sections and the
			    items. Agents editing by hand drift; the script also locks the file so parallel agents take turns.
			  </p></epic-aside
			>
			```
		</>
	</>

	<section label="3. Where it goes">
		<icon slot="icon" name="map"/>
		<text paragraph>
			<text bold>Its parents:</>
		</>
		<html>
			<ui-list bulleted>
				<ui-item>Anywhere prose goes: it's a <dfn class="spell-term" tabindex="0">prose element</><ui-popup heading="prose element" label="An <epic-*> element marked flow in its vocabulary:  it goes wherever prose goes, so no parent has to list it."></>: <ui-list bulleted><ui-item><ui-link target="src-packages-epics-docs-epic-item-html" link="/epic-item"><ui-text code>&lt;epic-item&gt;</></>: among an item's own text, before its cards</> <ui-item><ui-link target="src-packages-epics-docs-epic-answer-html" link="/epic-answer"><ui-text code>&lt;epic-answer&gt;</></>, <ui-link target="src-packages-epics-docs-epic-more-html" link="/epic-more"><ui-text code>&lt;epic-more&gt;</></>, <ui-link target="src-packages-epics-docs-epic-reply-html" link="/epic-reply"><ui-text code>&lt;epic-reply&gt;</></>: the cards under an item</> <ui-item><ui-link target="src-packages-epics-docs-epic-option-html" link="/epic-option"><ui-text code>&lt;epic-option&gt;</></>: an option card's pros and cons</> <ui-item><ui-link target="src-packages-epics-docs-epic-field-html" link="/epic-field"><ui-text code>&lt;epic-field&gt;</></>: a phase's field, or a labelled block</> <ui-item><ui-link target="src-packages-epics-docs-epic-updated-html" link="/epic-updated"><ui-text code>&lt;epic-updated&gt;</></>: a change to a phase's plan</> <ui-item><ui-link target="src-packages-epics-docs-epic-section-html" link="/epic-section"><ui-text code>&lt;epic-section&gt;</></>: an Overview sub-section's prose, or a report's</> <ui-item><ui-link target="src-packages-epics-docs-epic-version-html" link="/epic-version"><ui-text code>&lt;epic-version&gt;</></>: an earlier version, kept as it was</> <ui-item>another prose element (a note inside an aside), or plain HTML around it (a <ui-text code>&lt;li&gt;</>, a <ui-text code>&lt;div&gt;</>)</></></>
			</>
		</>
		<text paragraph>
			<text bold>Its children:</>
		</>
		<list bulleted>
			<item>prose: the aside</>
		</>
	</>

	<section label="4. Attributes">
