	<section label="5. How it looks">
		<icon slot="icon" name="palette"/>
		<list bulleted>
			<item>Its heading: always in full, as many lines as it needs, folded or open. The chevron and the slot's buttons sit on its first line, so nothing moves as it folds (2026-10-19).</>
			<item>No tooltip on its heading, folded or open: its words already say what it is, and name the button for a screen reader. ⌥-click still opens or folds everything inside (2026-11-20).</>
			<item>The brand's ivory panel, as the docs' asides (<text code>ui-accordion.spell-aside</>): warm, rounded, no border (<text code>--epic-aside</> from <text code>&lt;epic-page&gt;</>, with a fallback).</>
			<item>Its heading in the headings' italic serif, so it reads as an aside, not a section. Its text a step smaller than the page's.</>
			<item>No state colour: the ivory is the panel's, not a meaning.</>
			<item>Folded to start with. A click on the heading, or find-in-page, unfolds it; folding is the page's, never written.</>
			<item>It shares its shape with <text code>&lt;epic-code&gt;</> (<text code>EpicPanel</>, in the same family folder).</>
		</>
	</>

	<section label="6. Written by">
		<icon slot="icon" name="terminal"/>
		<list bulleted>
			<item>Claude writes it inside the HTML it passes to <text code>epic</> (<text code>add ... --details</>, <text code>decide --details</>, <text code>details --file</>, <text code>updated</>): no command makes one by itself.</>
			<item>The epic tool turns the OLD hand-shaped markup into this element, so a doc never holds the old shape. <list bulleted><item>It does this in any HTML a command takes: <text code>add --details</>, <text code>decide --details</>, <text code>details --file</>, <text code>updated</>.</> <item>The code that does it: <text code>IncomingHtml</> and <text code>ProseRewrite</>.</> <item>Prose edited by hand in a part file isn't passed through it.</> <item>The old shape: <text code>ui-accordion.spell-aside</>.</></></>
			<item>The converter did the same to every converted doc (<text code>ProseUpgrader</>).</>
		</>
	</>
	<html>
		<footer class="site-page-footer">
